    "documents_popup_alt": "ArSe. Archaeological Search",
    "documents_popup_content": "<p>The ArSe search engine (Archaeological Search) is a tool designed to locate publications related to archaeological research on the Iberian Peninsula. The tool allows you to locate words that appear in the text of publications, offering a preview of the context where those terms have been used. The search is carried out on articles from series published by different peninsular institutions whose contents are linked to this field of research. It includes books and articles edited by the Prehistory Museum of Valencia, the only case where access to the PDF of the document is also provided.<\/p><p>The series list offered by the search engine's dropdown constitutes the most updated reference of the titles on which the request is executed. It should be noted that only those titles that the editors offer openly on their respective pages are included, many of the series are not complete, and the process of including articles in ArSe is progressive, incorporating new references every week. Additionally, the indexing of some texts is complicated and their contents are not retrieved with the desired quality. Thus, the search results should serve as a guide for researchers and enthusiasts, but they should be interpreted with caution as they may be limited by various constraints.<\/p>",
    "documents_popup_title": "Archaeological publications search engine",
